    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger on successful owner create, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, reading the created owner (`@Val Owner`) and emitting id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** in `owners.POST.yml` as a new `audit` step placed *after* `save` (so the generated `id` is available) and before `respond`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors:\n\n```yaml\nsave:\n  ...\n  next: audit\n\naudit:\n  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AuditOwnerCreated\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\nThe audit line format:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07\n```\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The step follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (one public method, `@Val` state hand-off, governance listed on every covered step).",
